---
title: Genomic Contig Summary
sidebar:
  order: 11.1
---

Summary statistics for assembled contigs in FASTA format. For raw reads, see [Genomic Read Summary](/docs/api-usage/python/read_summary/).

## Example

```python
import pysegul

def summarize_contigs():
    summary = pysegul.ContigSummary(
        input_fmt='auto',
        output_dir='tests/output',
        output_prefix='contig_summary',
        )
    outputs = summary.from_dir('tests/contig-data')
```

To use a list of files, call `from_files` instead of `from_dir`:

```python
summary.from_files(['tests/contig-data/contig1.fasta', 'tests/contig-data/contig2.fasta'])
```

## Options

| Option | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `input_fmt` | Required | `'auto'`, `'fasta'`, `'gzip'` |
| `output_dir` | Required | Output directory |
| `output_prefix` | `None` | Name of the output files |
| `plot` *(beta)* | `None` | Chart options. See [Charts](#charts) |
| `checksum` | `None` | SHA-256 checksum mode in `report.json`: `'none'`, `'outputs'`, `'inputs'`, `'all'`, or `None` (`SEGUL_CHECKSUM`) |

## Methods

| Method | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `from_dir(input_dir)` | Summarize the contig files in a directory |
| `from_files(input_files)` | Summarize a list of contig files |

Both return a dictionary of output paths: `summary`, `report`, and `plots`.

## Charts

{% aside type="caution" title="Beta" %}
Charts are in beta and may still change.
{% /aside %}

Set `plot` to write charts to the `plots` folder of the output directory. See [Charts and Reports](/docs/api-usage/python/plots_reports/) for the chart options.

```python
summary = pysegul.ContigSummary(
    'auto',
    'tests/output',
    plot=pysegul.PlotOptions(format='svg'),
    )
outputs = summary.from_dir('tests/contig-data')
report = pysegul.load_contig_report(outputs['report'])
```
